**Global Naming Convention**
Noble Architecture code only — use `__` as the segment delimiter.

### Na__
Modules, filenames, JSON keys, DataLib identifiers.

### Na__AssemblyStudio__
All plugin source files and nested Ruby modules.

### na_
Ruby/JS methods, HtmlDialog callbacks, CSS classes, `@na_` ivars.

### NA_
Ruby constants (paths, tuning, naming contracts).

### Folders
`NN__Category__Subcategory__/`

### Files
`Na__AssemblyStudio__<Domain>__<Purpose>__.<ext>` — trailing `__` before extension.

### Ruby
`Na__AssemblyStudio.na_init`; config via `Na__AssemblyStudio__AppConfig__Main.json` + `Na__ConfigLoader.na_get`.

### JavaScript
`<script src>` in `Na__AssemblyStudio__UiLayout__.html`; IIFE → `window.Na__<System>__<Role>`; helpers `na_*`.

### Callbacks
Register `"na_*"`; newer door bridges may use camelCase on `window.sketchup`.

### Element IDs
`AWN###` / `ADR###` / `MOD###` per `DoorNamingContract` — not client project codes.
